        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Latex-ite Airport Grade is a solid mid-priced filler sealer that does its best work on sound, weathered asphalt that sees oil drips and real winters. It looks good, builds a meaningful film, and its fuel-resistance claim is useful in a garage apron. Its weaknesses are the ones shared by every thick DIY pail: lower coverage, heavier spreading and total dependence on prep and weather.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your driveway is in decent shape and you will put in a proper cleaning and crack-filling day first, it is a pail worth buying. If the surface is failing or brand new, put the money toward repair or patience instead, and come back to sealing when the asphalt is ready for it.
          </p>
        </div>

